<!-- ehos_app:readme -->
This application runs on [EHOS](https://github.com/EmpoweredHouse/eh-os), a platform for the
software a company runs its business on. Its business rules are written as contracts, in
`lib/<%= @app %>/contracts/`. EHOS deploys it from what `ehos.yaml` declares, and every action
taken through it is authorised and recorded. [VISION.md](VISION.md) says what that means for this
application.

`ehos_app`, the template the application was generated from, writes this section, and an upgrade
of the template rewrites it. The rest of the file is the application's.

## Quick start

<%= if @compose_database do %>You need [mise](https://mise.jdx.dev), Docker, which runs PostgreSQL from `compose.yaml`, and
`ehosctl`, the command-line tool for EHOS:<% else %>You need [mise](https://mise.jdx.dev), PostgreSQL 16 or later where `config/dev.exs` says, and
`ehosctl`, the command-line tool for EHOS:<% end %>

```sh
mise use -g github:EmpoweredHouse/ehos-tools   # ehosctl
mise install                                    # the Erlang and Elixir .tool-versions pins
mix setup                                       # dependencies, the database, the assets
mix phx.server
```

The application answers at [localhost:<%= @web_port %>](http://localhost:<%= @web_port %>), and
its health checks at `localhost:<%= @health_port %>/health/ready`. People sign in through EHOS;
locally, at the `/dev/sign-in` address the terminal prints ([DEVELOPMENT.md](DEVELOPMENT.md)), and
the tests sign in with a test credential.

## Everyday commands

| What | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Run the tests | `mix test` |
| Check everything before a commit | `mix precommit` |
| Check what CI checks, and have EHOS check `ehos.yaml` and the manifest | `ehosctl verify` |
| See the domain and its contracts as a tree | `mix ehos_contract.view --details` |
| Deploy a build | `ehosctl deploy <%= @ehos_name %> --env <env> --image <image> --manifest <file> [--graph <file>]…` |
| See whether the template, the engine or EHOS has a newer release | `ehosctl versions` |

How a change is made, built and deployed, step by step: [DEVELOPMENT.md](DEVELOPMENT.md).

